{%- set groups = atoms.atoms | priceGroups(priceGuideGroups, priceGuideExclude) -%}
<div class="answer">
  <p class="lead" style="color: var(--ink)">Most everyday things in Egypt cost tens to a few hundred Egyptian pounds: a metro ride is <bdi>{{ atoms.atoms.price_metro_single_journey | priceText }}</bdi>, a local restaurant meal <bdi>{{ atoms.atoms.price_local_restaurant | priceText }}</bdi> and a taxi from Cairo Airport to the centre <bdi>{{ atoms.atoms.price_airport_taxi | priceText }}</bdi>. The tables below give a fair range for each item, the month it was checked, and whether it is an official price or an InEgypt estimate.</p>
</div>
<p>InEgypt is a free iPhone app for visiting and getting around Egypt. It plans your trip day by day, finds routes by metro, train, bus and other public transport, and shows fair prices and common scams before you pay. These are the same prices the app shows, next to the place you are at.</p>
<p><b>How to read the tables.</b> Where a row says you can haggle, agree the price before the ride, tour or service starts. Official prices come with a link to the operator or the ministry; InEgypt estimates come from our own checks.</p>

{%- for g in groups %}
<h2>{{ g.title }}</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="facts-table">
  <caption>{{ g.title }}: fair price ranges</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Fair range</th><th scope="col">Haggle?</th><th scope="col">Checked and source</th></tr></thead>
